X: 1
T: Dentist!
O: Alan Menken, 1982
N: Orin's rockabilly number from Little Shop of Horrors. Melody is the top
N: voice of the piano channel in a hamienet.com MIDI (id 7939), key C minor as in
N: the source (range D4 to Eb5); chords fitted from the piano's left hand and,
N: for the hook (whose accompaniment in the source is melody plus drums only),
N: from the melody's own harmony. The intro riff's G3 and A3 are folded up an
N: octave for the recorder; the push syncopations are straightened to the eighth;
N: pitches are the source's. The source's boogie instrumental between verse and
N: hook is left out; its A and B naturals are written =A and =B over the C minor
N: key. Notated at double note values (quarters instead of eighths, eighths
N: instead of sixteenths) so the rockabilly eighths read plainly; the sounding
N: tempo is unchanged.
L: 1/8
Q: 1/2=120
M: 4/4
K: Cm
